            "text_5": "my shoulder locked up out of nowhere last fall. doctor said frozen shoulder, gave me cortisone, told me to stretch. cortisone wore off in two weeks. started this and by week 5 the shoulder started loosening. week 8 i put on my coat like a normal person. i actually laughed.",
            "image_url_5": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0732/4329/5930/files/w13.png?v=1776370450"
          }
        },
        {
          "type": "review_group",
          "settings": {
            "name_1": "Loretta A.",
            "rating_1": 5,
            "text_1": "my hands were so swollen some mornings i couldnt close them into a fist. rings didnt fit. typing at work was painful by noon. by week 6 the swelling reduced enough to wear my wedding ring again. by week 10 i was typing all day without pain. my rheumatologist asked what changed.",
